        <p>
          Operating system bloat often dictates hardware deprecation rather than physical failure. In an era where modern desktop environments demand multiple gigabytes of memory merely to reach an idle prompt, older compute nodes with strict hardware limitations are systematically abandoned.
        </p>

        <h3 class="fw-bold mt-4 mb-3" style="font-family: 'Roboto', sans-serif; font-size: 1.4rem; color: #111;">
          Analyzing Kernel Footprints
        </h3>
        <p>
          By inspecting baseline background daemons and tailoring minimal Unix systems, memory consumption can be dramatically curbed. Stripping non-essential background layers allows deterministic command execution and leaves the bulk of silicon capability available for compute-heavy local routines rather than cosmetic GUI overhead.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="p-3 my-4 border-start border-3 border-dark bg-light fst-italic">
          Software discipline remains the single most effective intervention against premature hardware obsolescence.
        </blockquote>

        <p>
